# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your key:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored. Never commit a real key.
# Get one at https://platform.claude.com/settings/keys

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ── Stripe (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All three, or none. With any one missing, the results page keeps saying
# "Checkout is not connected yet" and /stripe/webhook 404s — there is no
# half-live state, because a secret key without a webhook secret would take
# money and never grant access.
#
#   STRIPE_SECRET_KEY     sk_test_... from https://dashboard.stripe.com/apikeys
#   STRIPE_PRICE_ID       price_... for the $29/mo recurring price
#   STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET whsec_... printed by `stripe listen` or the dashboard
#
# The webhook endpoint is POST /stripe/webhook, and it MUST be subscribed to:
#
#   customer.subscription.created
#   customer.subscription.updated
#   customer.subscription.deleted
#
# `checkout.session.completed` alone is not enough and is the easy mistake:
# the session says a payment succeeded but carries no period end, and access
# hangs entirely on that date (see SubscriptionStore.isActive). Enable only
# that one and every customer pays and stays locked out — F21, arriving by
# configuration instead of by a dropped webhook. `npm run reconcile` repairs it
# within a day either way.
#
# Full walkthrough: docs/stripe-runbook.md. Then `npm run stripe:check`.
#
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# STRIPE_PRICE_ID=price_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...

# ── Being reachable from the internet ────────────────────────────────────────
# Setting BASE_URL to an https:// address is you telling the server it is
# public, and it then REFUSES TO START without the two below. Both faults are
# invisible when wrong, which is why it refuses rather than warns.
# Full walkthrough: docs/deploy-runbook.md
#
# USABILITY_LAB_BASE_URL=https://theusabilitylab.example
#
#   ...the gate cookie is a bearer credential and needs the Secure flag:
# USABILITY_LAB_SECURE_COOKIES=1
#
#   ...and behind a proxy every request arrives from the proxy, so the
#   per-client limit of five audits an hour would become five for the whole
#   site. Name the header your proxy writes; nothing is trusted by default.
# USABILITY_LAB_CLIENT_IP_HEADER=cf-connecting-ip
#
#   Bind to loopback so the proxy is the only way in. Without this the app also
#   answers on the LAN over plain http, where the Secure cookie is never sent
#   and the header above can be forged by anyone.
# USABILITY_LAB_BIND=127.0.0.1
#
#   Generated into out/.secret if unset. On a host with no persistent volume
#   that means every magic link and session dies on each deploy, silently.
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# USABILITY_LAB_SECRET=

# Mail. With no key every link is printed to the console instead of sent, which
# is what a fresh clone and the test suite both rely on — see src/mail.ts.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
#
# Unverified Resend accounts may send only from onboarding@resend.dev and only
# to the account owner's own address. That is enough to prove the flow; a custom
# From needs SPF and DKIM records on the domain.
# USABILITY_LAB_MAIL_FROM=hello@theusabilitylab.com
